# AI Assistants Never Mention Your Business

When customers ask ChatGPT or Perplexity for recommendations in your category, your competitors get cited and you don't.

Search is shifting from ranked links to generated answers. If your content isn't structured for AI retrieval, cited with real data, or consistently described across the web, AI engines simply have nothing reliable to quote when a prospect asks a question you could have answered.

Symptoms:
- Competitors show up in AI-generated answers and you don't
- No visibility into whether AI engines are even crawling your site
- Content written for keyword rankings but not structured as direct answers
- Inconsistent brand descriptions across your own site and third-party listings

Our solution: We restructure key pages with answer-first content, add the structured data AI systems parse, verify your site welcomes AI crawlers, and build the original data and consistent entity presence that earns citations instead of just rankings.

FAQs:

Q: Is GEO different from SEO?
A: They share a foundation but pursue different goals: SEO aims to rank, GEO aims to be cited and quoted directly by AI engines.

Q: How do I know if AI engines are crawling my site?
A: Server logs will show user agents like GPTBot, ClaudeBot, or PerplexityBot; if they're absent or blocked, that's the first thing to fix.